Z||000000||Master_Sushi||02-05-2001||12:46 PM||||Ok, I just installed a new motor from autozone, and my wipers STILL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> dont go down like they should. Is there anything else I can check? Any relays or fuses? Please help...... Getting sick of not driving my fiero due to windshield wipers being off.||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||02-05-2001||05:54 PM||||do the wipers stop in the same place and where exactly are they stopping if they do?||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||02-05-2001||07:07 PM||||mine don't go down all the way like they should either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||02-06-2001||01:06 AM||||My wipers dont park at all. They work every other way fine. I replaced the motor and they still dont park at all, or even try to. Is there anything else I should be checking? Maybe the stalk? I checked all the wires with a meter. They are all fine, I could see the park was triggering. I'm just running out of ideas now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||02-06-2001||07:56 AM||||does the wiper stroke the windshield the way its supposed to? If it stops in same place all the time just above where its supposed to, maybe you dont have the arm in the rite place on shaft. just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||02-06-2001||12:46 PM||||roger, how can i adjust the arms? do i need to get one of those tools to pull them off then put them back on?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||02-06-2001||01:53 PM||||they just slide onto splined shafts. I use a flat screwdriver and another one laying on cowl to act as a pivot. Just catch the edge of wiper arm at shaft and pry it off. to put it back just move it where you want it but dont push down hard all the way till your sure, then push it till it locks. when it pops loose be ready to catch it before it flies up and scratches your hood.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||02-06-2001||04:21 PM||||There's a much easire way to remove the wiper arms. Pull back the arm and put a small nail or wire in the hole near the hinge pin. The arms now stay back by themselves, now just lift the little silver tab at the base and lift the arm off.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||02-06-2001||06:13 PM||||thanks for the info guys. they look a lot better now.||||reg||1
